  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID-Wildlife Security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to protect apes, elephants and other endangered species in nine countries from illegal trade by increasing the level of wildlife law enforcement in the Central and West African regions and deterring potential traders from conducting these illegal activities. The project will: 1) Ignite the replication of the LAGA model for NGO-government collaboration on wildlife law enforcement in four more countries in collaboration with partner NGOs, 2) Set precedence of landmark first deterring wildlife prosecution of a major wildlife criminal in four countries, 3) Enable NGO partners to have full ownership functioning sustainable national projects of wildlife law enforcement setting four countries on - one arrest per week - enforcement rate, creating .a block of nine countries with functioning enforcement in the region; 4) Establish a model for Sub-regional Wildlife Law Enforcement on the five broad activities of investigations, arrest operations, legal assistance, media promotion and reporting.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
